Timothy, I understand you are Australian.  if the link you provided is inde=
ed how you pronounce "on", then it will probably be confused with the lojba=
n "a".  It's closer to how that same website pronounces "north".  It should=
 be basically be around either here<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Close-mid=
_back_rounded_vowel>: or here<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open-mid_back_r=
ounded_vowel> or in-between<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mid_back_rounded_=
vowel> (always rounded lips) whereas a hangs around either here<https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/Open_front_unrounded_vowel> or here<https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/Open_back_unrounded_vowel> or in-between<https://en.wikipedia.org=
/wiki/Open_central_unrounded_vowel> always with lips unrounded.

             --gejyspa


